</style>
<style>@page { size: 900,00pt 664,50pt; margin: 0 }</style></head>
<body>
<h1>DATA PIPELINE: THREE DISTINCT DISCIPLINES</h1>
<div class="sub">structuring → normalization → harmonization</div>
<div class="col root"><div class="row"><div class="card blue"><div class="t">1. STRUCTURING</div><div class="d">raw → readable format</div>
<div class="d"></div>
<div class="d">unstructured</div>
<div class="d">~@#)($&amp;</div>
<div class="d">xyz___??!!</div>
<div class="d">(((raw)))</div>
<div class="d"></div>
<div class="d">structured table</div>
<div class="d">| id | name | email |</div>
<div class="d">| 1 | Alice | a@x.com |</div>
<div class="d">| 2 | Bob | b@y.com |</div>
<div class="d">| 3 | Carol | c@z.com |</div>
<div class="d"></div>
<div class="d">WHY IT MATTERS</div>
<div class="d">Machine-readable format for queries</div>
<div class="d"></div>
<div class="d"></div>
<div class="d"></div>
<div class="d"></div>
<div class="d"></div>
<div class="d"></div>
<div class="d"></div>
<div class="d"></div></div>
<div class="arrow">&#8594;</div>
<div class="card blue"><div class="t">2. NORMALIZATION</div><div class="d">clean + deduplicate + rescale</div>
<div class="d"></div>
<div class="d">A. Database (1NF→2NF→3NF)</div>
<div class="d">1NF: atomic values, unique rows</div>
<div class="d">2NF: no partial dependencies</div>
<div class="d">3NF: no transitive dependencies</div>
<div class="d"></div>
<div class="d">B. Statistical / ML</div>
<div class="d">Min-Max</div>
<div class="d">[0 .. 1]</div>
<div class="d">Z-Score</div>
<div class="d">μ=0, σ=1</div>
<div class="d"></div>
<div class="d">EXAMPLE</div>
<div class="d">Source A: DD/MM/YYYY → 2026-09-15</div>
<div class="d">Source B: YYYY-MM-DD → 2026-09-15</div>
<div class="d">A:&quot;USA&quot; + B:&quot;United States&quot; → &quot;United States&quot;</div>
<div class="d">EUR ↔ USD → uniform scale</div>
<div class="d"></div>
<div class="d"></div>
<div class="d"></div>
<div class="d"></div></div>
<div class="arrow">&#8594;</div>
<div class="card green"><div class="t">3. HARMONIZATION</div><div class="d">multi-source → semantic unity</div>
<div class="d"></div>
<div class="d">Source A</div>
<div class="d">Source B</div>
<div class="d">Source C</div>
<div class="d"></div>
<div class="d">UNIFIED VIEW</div>
<div class="d">✓ consistent schemas</div>
<div class="d">✓ uniform standards</div>
<div class="d">✓ semantic unity</div>
<div class="d">comparable + error-free</div>
<div class="d"></div>
<div class="d">Integration</div>
<div class="d">data in one place</div>
<div class="d">(just gathering)</div>
<div class="d">Harmonization</div>
<div class="d">+ resolves conflicts</div>
<div class="d">+ semantic unity</div>
<div class="d"></div>
<div class="d">THE BOTTOM LINE</div>
<div class="d">Don't just structure. Don't just normalize.</div>
<div class="d">Aim for HARMONIZATION.</div></div></div>
<div><div style="font-weight:700;font-size:15px">THE LIFECYCLE: MULTI-SOURCE PIPELINE (cycles repeat)</div></div>
<div class="row"><div class="card blue"><div class="t">INGESTION</div><div class="d">structuring (1st pass)</div>
<div class="d"></div></div>
<div class="arrow">&#8594;</div>
<div class="card blue"><div class="t">TRANSFORMATION</div><div class="d">normalization (clean + scale)</div></div>
<div class="arrow">&#8594;</div>
<div class="card blue"><div class="t">LOADING</div><div class="d">structuring (2nd pass)</div>
<div class="d"></div></div>
<div class="arrow">&#8594;</div>
<div class="card green"><div class="t">HARMONIZATION</div><div class="d">all 3 combined, cycled per batch</div></div></div>
<div><div style="font-size:14px;color:var(--ink2)">↻ repeat per data batch</div></div>
<div><div style="font-size:13px;color:var(--ink2)">#DataEngineering #DataScience #DataHarmonization #MachineLearning #SystemArchitecture</div></div></div>


</body>
</html>
